---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on Plans65: none are set, and how you can verify it" description="Plans65 sets no cookie and stores nothing on your device: no tracking pixel, no advertising tag, no lead capture. How to check it yourself in the developer tools of your browser." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>No cookie is set by this site and no local storage is used. Your county, income or drug costs live only in the open page, and in its address if you copy a share link.</p>
    <h2>Why there is no banner</h2>
    <p>A consent banner is needed when a site stores or reads non-essential information on your device. Nothing like that happens here. {CLARITY_ID ? 'The cookie-free stability monitoring described in the privacy policy stores nothing on your device either.' : 'No analytics or advertising script is loaded.'}</p>
    <h2>Check it</h2>
    <p>Open the developer tools of your browser (F12), then the Application or Storage tab: under Cookies and Local Storage, this site stays empty while you use the plan finder. In the Network tab, choosing another state downloads one public file named after the state, and nothing else leaves your device.</p>
    <p>More in the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
